[00:08.32]1. Jehovah God, I call to you and ask you:
[00:16.64]“Hear my prayer.”
[00:24.96]My wounds are deep and slow to heal;
[00:31.44]my load is hard to bear.
[00:35.68]Despondent thoughts and disappointed hopes
[00:39.76]have left me weak.
[00:43.92]O God of comfort, care for me;
[00:47.25]your favor I do seek.
[00:50.58](Chorus)
[00:53.92]Do raise me up; help me endure.
[01:03.36]When I’m in doubt, make my hope sure.
[01:12.38]From deep despair, I turn to you.
[01:20.16]Jehovah God, my strength renew.
[01:40.99]2. Your Word has been my comfort and
[01:46.65]a refuge when I’m weak,
[01:51.15]Expressing feelings dear to me
[01:55.65]in words I cannot speak.
[01:58.32]Please build in me the faith and trust
[02:00.98]that your Word does impart.
[02:04.60]And help me always know your love
[02:09.35]is greater than my heart.
[02:14.10](Chorus)
[02:20.10]Do raise me up; help me endure.
[02:27.16]When I’m in doubt, make my hope sure.
[02:35.96]From deep despair, I turn to you.
[02:59.78]Jehovah God, my strength renew.